// SR 444.11 — Section 4 Guarantee of Return
// generated by src/parse.py. Do not edit by hand.

:NOTE
English is not an official language of the Swiss Confederation. This translation is provided for information purposes only and has no legal force.

:INFO
Art. 7
1 The institution borrowing one or more items of cultural property must submit a request for the issue of a guarantee of return to the specialist service, at the latest three months before the intended import of the cultural property into Switzerland.
2 The request must include the following information:
a. name and address of the lending institution;
b. a description of the cultural property;
c. as precise a description as possible of the cultural property’s origin;
d. the intended date of the temporary import of cultural property into Switzerland;
e. the intended date of the export of the cultural property from Switzerland;
f. the duration of the exhibition;
g. the requested term of the guarantee of return.
3 The request must be submitted in an official language. The information specified in paragraph 2 letters b and c must be submitted in electronic form. This information may also be submitted in English.
|

:INFO
Art. 7 (continued)
4 A loan agreement signed by all parties must be enclosed with the request. The agreement must indicate that the cultural property will be returned to the contracting state from which it was borrowed at the end of the exhibition in Switzerland or at the end of a travelling exhibition through multiple countries.
5 The specialist service shall allow the borrowing institution a period of ten days to rectify incomplete requests or requests submitted without the loan agreement. It shall combine the deadline with the warning that the request may be rejected without publication (Art. 11 para. 2 CPTA) if the request is not rectified within the deadline or the loan agreement is not submitted.
|

:INFO
Art. 7 (continued)
6 The validity of a legally binding guarantee of return may be extended once by a maximum of four months in the event of an exhibition extension, provided that the exhibition period is extended without interruption. In order to extend the validity of the guarantee of return, the borrowing institution must submit confirmation of the extension of the loan period from the lending institution to the specialist service.
|

:NOTE
Para. 2 let. c — Amended by No I of the O of 15 Oct. 2025, in force since 1 Jan. 2026 (AS 2025 634).
Para. 4 — Amended by No I of the O of 15 Oct. 2025, in force since 1 Jan. 2026 (AS 2025 634).
Para. 5 — Amended by No I of the O of 15 Oct. 2025, in force since 1 Jan. 2026 (AS 2025 634).
Para. 6 — Inserted by No I of the O of 15 Oct. 2025, in force since 1 Jan. 2026 (AS 2025 634).

